      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for those. character 1's dialogue feels very sharp and professional, which is exactly what we want. \n\nbut for character 2, the dialogue feels a bit... too clean? it reads a lot like a standard textbook or a news report. since this is a gritty drama, i was hoping the character's voice would sound more \"grounded\" in their specific environment. \n\nin the neighborhoods we're profiling, people don't really use quite that much formal syntax. could you rewrite character 2's lines using more authentic, colloquial language? i want to capture the specific rhythm and dialect of a working-class urban environment—maybe someone who grew up in that area and uses more localized speech patterns or slang. i think it'll make the character feel much more \"real\" and help the audience immediately grasp their social identity and the stakes they're facing.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
